ith a reason for every requested id; DISMISS additionally takes only out-of-scope, refuted, or not-worth-cost and a reason. Missing, duplicate, unrequested, malformed, or incomplete content refuses; no value is defaulted.\"","+detail = \"kitlib.dispute accepts one TOML findings file with only a non-empty `range` and a non-empty `[[finding]]` list. Each finding has exactly a unique letter-led id, held_by `builder` or `coordinator`, and non-empty finding and position text, which the reader keeps verbatim apart from every leading and trailing newline character; spaces and interior lines are kept. request_line writes the composed request, and requested_ids reads its first DISPUTE findings line. parse reads RULING lines one physical line at a time and accepts only one FIX, DISMISS, or ESCALATE ruling with a reason for every requested id; DISMISS additionally takes only out-of-scope, refuted, or not-worth-cost and a reason. Missing, duplicate, unrequested, malformed, or incomplete content refuses; no value is defaulted.\""," rationale = \"Both adjudication routes need one grammar for the coordinator's findings input and the adjudicator's verdict. A single parser prevents a composed brief, entry point, and later loop sitting from accepting different finding sets or verdict meanings.\""," test_refs = \"TC-334\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"," "]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-865\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3378,"oldLines":10,"newStart":3378,"newLines":10,"lines":[" [test.TC-334]"," verifies = [\"SR-234\", \"LLR-314\", \"LLR-315\", \"IF-290\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Run the dispute tests that compose a brief carrying every finding, held position, range fact and review-scope link; refuse malformed findings input; parse a complete verdict; refuse malformed, incomplete, duplicated, unrequested, or unbound verdicts; prove an accepted dispute verdict authorizes no approval act; and prove the class is routed through its shipped template. Run the coordinator-entry tests that accept the dispute class, bind every requested finding, reject an unruled finding, and refuse a dispute brief naming no findings before launch.\"","+method = \"Run the dispute tests that compose a brief carrying every finding, held position, range fact and review-scope link; refuse malformed findings input, including a finding with an extra key and one missing any of id, held_by, finding, or position, each by name without a brief; parse a complete verdict; refuse malformed, incomplete, duplicated, unrequested, or unbound verdicts; prove an accepted dispute verdict authorizes no approval act; and prove the class is routed through its shipped template. Run the coordinator-entry tests that accept the dispute class, bind every requested finding, reject an unruled finding, and refuse a dispute brief naming no findings before launch.\""," tier = \"Smoke\"","-expected = \"A dispute brief contains every requested finding and position verbatim with independently derived range facts and a review-scope link, or refuses without a partial brief. Its verdict accepts exactly one reasoned declared ruling for every requested finding and no other; an accepted dispute verdict authorizes no approval act. The coordinator entry point binds the requested findings and refuses an empty request before launch.\"","+expected = \"A dispute brief contains every requested finding and position verbatim with independently derived range facts and a review-scope link, or refuses without a partial brief. A finding with an extra key or one missing any of id, held_by, finding, or position refuses by name without a brief. Its verdict accepts exactly one reasoned declared ruling for every requested finding and no other; an accepted dispute verdict authorizes no approval act. The coordinator entry point binds the requested findings and refuses an empty request before launch.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_dispute.py::test_the_dispute_brief_carries_each_finding_its_position_range_and_scope_link;tests/test_dispute.py::test_a_malformed_findings_file_refuses_the_brief;tests/test_dispute.py::test_a_well_formed_verdict_is_accepted_and_parsed;tests/test_dispute.py::test_a_malformed_or_incomplete_verdict_is_refused;tests/test_dispute.py::test_a_verdict_judged_against_no_requested_findings_is_refused;tests/test_dispute.py::test_an_accepted_dispute_verdict_authorizes_no_approval_act;tests/test_dispute.py::test_the_dispute_class_is_routed_and_its_template_ships;tests/test_coordinator_adjudicate.py::test_the_entry_point_accepts_the_dispute_class;tests/test_coordinator_adjudicate.py::test_a_dispute_verdict_ruling_every_finding_is_valid_and_bound;tests/test_coordinator_adjudicate.py::test_a_dispute_verdict_leaving_a_finding_unruled_fails;tests/test_coordinator_adjudicate.py::test_a_dispute_brief_naming_no_findings_is_refused_before_launch\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-865\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3321,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3321,"newLines":7,"lines":[" detail = \"kitlib.dispute accepts one TOML findings file with only a non-empty `range` and a non-empty `[[finding]]` list. Each finding has exactly a unique letter-led id, held_by `builder` or `coordinator`, and non-empty finding and position text, which the reader keeps verbatim apart from every leading and trailing newline character; spaces and interior lines are kept. request_line writes the composed request, and requested_ids reads its first DISPUTE findings line. parse reads RULING lines one physical line at a time and accepts only one FIX, DISMISS, or ESCALATE ruling with a reason for every requested id; DISMISS additionally takes only out-of-scope, refuted, or not-worth-cost and a reason. Missing, duplicate, unrequested, malformed, or